    {
      "id": "https://www.dezeen.com/2026/10/05/plat-life-nature-of-design-ngv-melbourne/",
      "url": "https://www.dezeen.com/2026/10/05/plat-life-nature-of-design-ngv-melbourne/",
      "title": "[Dezeen] Plant Life exhibition imagines a future where \"plants return as the dominant source\"",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"http://static.dezeen.com/uploads/2026/10/ngv-plant-life-the-nature-of-design-exhibition-biomaterial-melbourne-australia_dezeen_1704_col_sq-411x411.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p>From a fire jacket grown from fungi to building blocks made from algae and oyster shells, the latest exhibition at Melbourne's National Gallery of Victoria (NGV) explores humanity's relationship with the plant world through design. Called Plant Life: The Nature of Design, the exhibition features more than 60 works that span furniture, architecture, decorative arts,</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.dezeen.com/2026/10/05/plat-life-nature-of-design-ngv-melbourne/\">Plant Life exhibition imagines a future where \"plants return as the dominant source\"</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.dezeen.com\">Dezeen</a>.</p>",
      "date_published": "2026-10-05T09:00:25+00:00",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Dezeen",
          "url": "https://www.dezeen.com"
        }
      ],
      "image": "http://static.dezeen.com/uploads/2026/10/ngv-plant-life-the-nature-of-design-exhibition-biomaterial-melbourne-australia_dezeen_1704_col_sq-411x411.jpg",
      "_score": 48,
