    {
      "id": "https://www.archdaily.com/1186151/casa-vereda",
      "url": "https://www.archdaily.com/1186151/casa-vereda",
      "title": "[ArchDaily] Casa Vereda / L'Aura Ortín Architecture for Happiness",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://images.adsttc.com/media/images/6abe/778d/07c3/d100/017f/c448/large_jpg/2.jpg?1790867418\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p>Casa Vereda stems from a simple idea: to inhabit nature without competing with it. The project blends into the landscape through an architecture that seeks to become part of its surroundings. Volumes, materials, and textures engage in a dialogue with vegetation, light, and the memory of the place, creating a house that seems to have always been there.</p>",
      "date_published": "2026-10-03T16:00:00+00:00",
