    {
      "id": "https://www.archdaily.com/1034708/monte-alvo-house-noz-arquitectura",
      "url": "https://www.archdaily.com/1034708/monte-alvo-house-noz-arquitectura",
      "title": "[ArchDaily] Monte Alvo House / NOZ Arquitectura",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://images.adsttc.com/media/images/68e0/30b8/e5d9/cd01/88b3/025e/large_jpg/monte-alvo-house-noz-arquitectura_17.jpg?1759523012\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p>The architectural tradition of the Alentejo is defined by <strong>simplicity of form, functional spaces, and a deep connection with climate and landscape</strong>. At the top of Monte Alvo, the house is single-story, positioned to make full use of solar orientation and ensure thermal comfort throughout the year.</p>",
      "date_published": "2026-10-03T13:00:00+00:00",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "ArchDaily",
          "url": "https://www.archdaily.com"
        }
      ],
      "image": "https://images.adsttc.com/media/images/68e0/30b8/e5d9/cd01/88b3/025e/large_jpg/monte-alvo-house-noz-arquitectura_17.jpg?1759523012",
      "_score": 40,
      "_quality": 58,
